    <section class="mx-auto max-w-screen-2xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mt-16 lg:mt-24">
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
            <span class="eyebrow">
                <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-orange-100"></span>
                Compare
            </span>
            <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Less code. Less context-switching.</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 muted text-lg">
                In pure PHP, every source and sink has its own functions, error model, and memory
                tradeoffs. With Flow, the pipeline shape stays constant - swap the source or sink
                and the rest of the code doesn't budge.
            </p>
